      "sha256": "bfc70cc646bbe0faee7adca4d6dd1af2befa3aef5924bf612c2538478e60790c",
      "prompt": "Create production-ready transparent furniture sprite layers for the pure-2D narrative game NEURONS. Image 1 is an ORIENTATION/SCALE/REGISTRATION guide with a 3-column by 2-row grid of six items. Images 2 and 3 are approved PAINTING/VIEWPOINT style references only: dusty warm wood against grey-violet shadows, broad restrained hand-painted gouache/oil-like color masses, expressive selective brush edges, believable everyday joinery and quiet wear. Do not copy their room layout or add any room. Replace the primitive-looking guide silhouettes with complete, beautifully painted usable furniture sprites, maintaining each item's same cell, apparent footprint, oblique camera, long-axis direction, approximate size and bottom registration. Treat the guide only as orientation/scale support, not the final surface or aesthetic. Preserve open spaces between legs and cabinet shelves. All objects use the SAME fixed oblique three-quarter elevated camera: world horizontal axes nearly horizontal gently rising right, depth running down-right; visible west and south faces. No frontal UI icons, no top-down, no diamond-isometric redesign, no room floor. Exactly three equal columns, two equal rows, isolated non-touching sprites and truly transparent empty background, no text/grid/borders/shadows. Cell order: TOP LEFT a low ordinary worn wooden single bed, long axis running left-right exactly as the guide, headboard at the LEFT end, simple sturdy thin frame and four feet, a cream mattress and one soft used pillow, NO blanket; TOP MIDDLE a small warm dark-wood bedside cabinet CARCASS, visible top and two side walls with three EMPTY open drawer bays, no drawer fronts or movable objects; TOP RIGHT a simple old wooden writing desk with thin rounded-edge top, four true legs, believable modest joinery and side apron, EMPTY surface with no book/lamp/paper; BOTTOM LEFT a separate matching wooden chair with thin seat, gently shaped backrest, four independent legs and clear negative space; BOTTOM MIDDLE ONE open wooden drawer tray with its front panel and restrained brass pull, internal tray sidewalls visible, perspective and wood matching the bedside carcass, no cabinet, no other drawers; BOTTOM RIGHT ONE subdued grey-blue soft bed blanket resting in the exact same plane/orientation as the bed guide, a separate detachable layer with a couple of broad fabric creases and a small draped near edge, no bed/mattress/pillow underneath. Painterly internal form shading only; no cast shadow or ground reflection beyond each sprite, no props baked onto furniture, no person, no glow, no sparkles, no unrelated objects, no photographic/PBR finish, no dense random texture. Preserve all full item edges and feet with generous transparent cell margins. Warm muted local illumination consistent across all six layers, no spotlight.\n",
      "tool": "built_in_image_gen",
      "transparent_background": true,
