      "prompt": "Create production-ready transparent furniture sprite layers for the pure-2D narrative game NEURONS. Image 1 is an ORIENTATION/SCALE/REGISTRATION guide containing 3 columns by 2 rows. Images 2 and 3 are approved STYLE/CAMERA references only: dusty warm browns, quiet grey-violet shadows, restrained painterly oil/gouache color masses, selective irregular brush edges, believable worn household materials. Do not reproduce a room or any furniture placement. Paint complete expressive usable furniture from the guide, preserving each item's grid cell, apparent footprint, long-axis direction, scale and registration. The guide is not the final aesthetic: replace its rigid flat primitive appearance with real joinery, rounded everyday forms and selective painterly detail. Same fixed elevated oblique camera for every item, horizontal direction gently rising right and depth down-right; show the left-facing WEST and front SOUTH surfaces. No frontal icons or top-down. Exactly THREE equal columns and TWO equal rows, no grids/borders/labels, transparent negative space. Cells in reading order: TOP LEFT an old grey-teal metal standing electric fan BODY with a slender pole, round weighted foot and complete fine-wire safety cage, EMPTY cage with no fan blades/rotor inside (rotor is a separate layer below), exact orientation and size of the guide; TOP MIDDLE an EMPTY warm brown wooden standing coat rack with a rounded mast, branching curved hooks and three stable feet, no clothes/bags/coat; TOP RIGHT a narrow old wooden BOOKCASE whose opening faces LEFT as the guide, long footprint depth extending DOWN-RIGHT, genuine open shelves and varied muted book spines inside, believable side boards and thin shelves with empty gaps rather than a solid rectangular box; BOTTOM LEFT a plain worn tall wooden WARDROBE with two CLOSED subtly raised-panel doors, restrained small pulls, visible left-facing front, narrow depth side face, simple plinth, no clothes or objects outside; BOTTOM MIDDLE the detached THREE metal fan blades plus small central hub ONLY, oriented and scaled for the fan body's cage, no cage/stand/floor, with transparent empty space between the three curved blades, internal paint shading but no motion blur; BOTTOM RIGHT the SAME wardrobe with doors OPEN enough to reveal its EMPTY interior and hanging rail, same identity/dimensions/registration/perspective/wood as the closed wardrobe, no clothes or loose objects. Every sprite must be fully visible, separated from neighbours by generous transparent margins. True alpha background with no floor, environment, cast shadows, checkerboard, person, labels, glow, extra objects or photographic shine. Use broad calm painterly forms and limited selected wear, not all-over procedural scratches or uniform high-frequency noise.\n",
